--TEST--
A file starts in text mode and every byte outside the tags is written verbatim, `<?nvs` opens code mode and `?>` closes it, `?>` swallows one following newline, `<?= expr ?>` writes one value where it stands, a `{ … }` block may begin in one mode and end in the other, and neither `<?` nor `<?xml` is an open tag (`rule:statements/nvs-is-the-only-open-tag`)
--FILE--
before
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/code-mode-and-html-mode
// The file above this tag was text mode: those bytes went out as they stood.
string $who = "world";
?>
after <?= $who ?>!
<?nvs
// `rule:statements/nvs-is-the-only-open-tag`: there is no short open tag, so
// neither of the next two lines is code.
?>
<? not an open tag ?>
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?nvs
// A `?>` takes the single newline directly after it, so the line below this
// tag starts where the text starts rather than after a blank line.
?>
no blank line above
<?nvs
// A block may open in code mode, hold page text, and close in code mode.
array<string> $products = ["pen", "ink"];
foreach ($products as string $name) {
?>
  <li><?= $name ?></li>
<?nvs
}
?>
end
--EXPECT--
before
after world!
<? not an open tag ?>
<?xml version="1.0"?>
no blank line above
  <li>pen</li>
  <li>ink</li>
end
